180	 * The check runs per shell segment (via {@link splitShellCommands}) so that a
181	 * package-manager phrase inside a QUOTED argument — a commit message, echoed
182	 * help text — is treated as data, not a command; and each segment is
183	 * backslash-unescaped first so escaped executable names cannot slip past. A
184	 * segment matches if it starts with a denied prefix or matches an install
185	 * pattern.
