210	 * "command not found" (exit 127) no matter how it is spelled or wrapped
211	 * (`"nix" run`, `env nix`, `sh -c '…'`, `git -c alias=!nix`), because the
212	 * lookup is on the RESOLVED binary name, which quoting cannot change. So this
213	 * detector canonicalizes quoting for good coverage of the common cases but
214	 * treats any miss as a UX gap, not a hole.
215	 */
